Status
Accepted

Context

CyberLab requires an extensible mechanism that allows new capabilities to be
added without modifying the Core application.

Decision

Adopt a plugin architecture based on Python Entry Points.

Plugins are discovered through EntryPointProvider, instantiated by
PluginLoader and stored by PluginRegistry.

Consequences

Positive

- Extensible platform.
- No Core modifications required for new plugins.
- Small and cohesive responsibilities.
- Compatible with Clean Architecture.
- Compatible with Hexagonal Architecture.

Negative

- Requires Python packaging metadata.
- Plugins must comply with PluginProtocol.

Alternatives Considered

PluginManager

Rejected because it centralizes multiple responsibilities.

CapabilityRegistry

Rejected because no current use case justifies its existence.

EntryPointProviderProtocol

Rejected because the dependency remains entirely inside Infrastructure,
making an additional abstraction unnecessary.

Future Evolution

The same architecture may support:

- Official plugins
- Community plugins
- Plugin SDK
- Marketplace
- Remote plugin repositories

without requiring architectural redesign.
